l Rasputin.<br /> <br /> But there are definitely lots of unintentional contradictions between game lines. And a fair amount of intentional contradictions when later writers/developers wanted to piss all over what was previously established.<br /> <br /> So canon isn't even canon. Though talking about it can be productive to determine what you want in your own chronicles. Take what you find useful and discard the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T11:39:26-07:00","id":1415709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1415461-problems-in-the-wod-timeline?p=1415480#post1415480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironic, considering the setting has actual time police.</div> </div> </div> </div>The chrononuts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T22:48:42-07:00","id":1416686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1415461-problems-in-the-wod-timeline?p=1415471#post1415471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different WoD books contradict each other - this is why there are like seven or eight versions of Rasputin in the setting. I was wondering if anyone had a list of such issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. Did not some books state that what's written within about the world and it's history is only from the viewpoint of a member of that Clan / kind of being? So there isn't any &quot;truth&quot; at all, but only what members of that society might learn by it's other members.<br /> <br /> Ok, with some books even this explanation is a problem, like when deep hidden knowledge was within, which only very few or no-one at all had. Like the whole Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand book, any Noddhist books or knowledge about Tremere's soul etc...<br /> <br /> What also caused contradictions were things that got declared &quot;out of canon&quot; in a later revision. Mostly this was done by stating that the old knowledge were only rumors. (like Vicissitude mutating it's users to Souleater NPCs.)<br /> <br /> Another explanation which is hinted in Romans and background stories are the (mass) memory altering effects caused by mind disciplines like Dominate through Metusaleh over a very long time. Most other supernatural beings (Mages, Faerie, Wolvis) have their own variants of these..<br /> <br /> With True Brujah 